<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.10.7: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02508</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.10.7: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e604e538-5c73-4d6b-b90a-c2361fb84f54</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
        <exercise id="_8c25877c-9dbc-44e7-861f-f5cf0ed3b65f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00002">Select three statements that are true about the graph of this function.</para>
            <para id="para-00003">The following quadratic expressions all define the same function.</para>
            <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00007">Correct! The vertex is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00008">Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.1.</para>
            <para id="para-00009">The correct answers are: The vertex is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d1b254ae-9370-478e-a72b-d731b6830440" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00010">Enter the value of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate.</para>
            <para id="para-00011">The following expressions all define the same quadratic function.</para>
            <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>24</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>25</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00015">What is the value of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> of the graph of the function?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00016">Correct! The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>24</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00017">Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.1.</para>
            <para id="para-00018">The correct answer is -24. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>24</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="bbf0723e-dd5f-4632-8aaf-6419c4973eec" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00019"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts of the graph.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00020">Correct! The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts of the graph are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00021">Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.1.</para>
            <para id="para-00022">The correct answers are: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts of the graph are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_8868d88b-2575-4438-9a84-f97e79918f49" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00023">Enter the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate.</para>
            <para id="para-00024">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of the graph?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00025">Correct! The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is -1.</para>
            <para id="para-00026">Try again. Revisit activities 9.10.1 and 9.10.6.</para>
            <para id="para-00027">The correct answer is -1. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is -1.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="e8df213e-14b1-4b54-8b38-fe140f2a3865" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00028">Enter the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate.</para>
            <para id="para-00029">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of the graph?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00030">Correct! The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is -25.</para>
            <para id="para-00031">Try again. Revisit activities 9.10.1 and 9.10.6.</para>
            <para id="para-00032">The correct answer is -25. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex graph is -25.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="faee25e1-e05c-447b-b41d-a7a8cb448a5f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00033">Is this an accurate graph of the function?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00034">Correct! Yes. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept, and vertex are plotted accurately.</para>
            <para id="para-00035">Try again. Revisit activities 9.10.1 and 9.10.6.</para>
            <para id="para-00036">The correct answer is Yes. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept, and vertex are plotted accurately.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_023b0c87-8a26-40f5-822f-bc7e5d89c329" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00037">Original expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00038">Here is one way an expression in standard form is rewritten into vertex form.</para>
            <para id="para-00039"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00040"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>49</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00041"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>24</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>49</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00042"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>25</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00043">In Step 1, where did the number <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> come from?</para>
            <para id="para-00044">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00045">It is the substitute value for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00046">Every term in the expression was divided by 2.</para>
            <para id="para-00047">It is half of -7 being squared.</para>
            <para id="para-00048">Only the non-linear term was divided by 2.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00049">Correct! It is half of -7 being squared.</para>
            <para id="para-00050">Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00051">The correct answer is: It is half of -7 being squared.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="f4e40af1-4c16-4820-9742-55da706419ba" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            <para id="para-00052">In Step 1, why was <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> added and then subtracted?</para>
            <para id="para-00053">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00054">It is added to complete the square. It is subtracted to keep the value of the expression unchanged.</para>
            <para id="para-00055">It is subtracted to complete the square. It is added to keep the value of the expression unchanged.</para>
            <para id="para-00056">It is added to complete the square. It is subtracted to change the value of the expression.</para>
            <para id="para-00057">It is subtracted to complete the square. It is added to change the value of the expression.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            <para id="para-00058">Correct! It is added to complete the square. It is subtracted to keep the value of the expression unchanged.</para>
            <para id="para-00059">Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00060">The correct answer is: It is added to complete the square. It is subtracted to keep the value of the expression unchanged.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="a9cb3566-dd50-4111-9c3d-4dd33e0f0626" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00009">
            <para id="para-00061">What happened in Step 2?</para>
            <para id="para-00062">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00063">The expression is subtracted to keep the value of the expression unchanged.</para>
            <para id="para-00064">The expression, which is a perfect square, is written as a squared expression.</para>
            <para id="para-00065">The expression, which is not a perfect square, is written as a squared expression.</para>
            <para id="para-00066">The expression is added to keep the value of the expression unchanged.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00009">
            <para id="para-00067">Correct! The expression, which is a perfect square, is written as a squared expression.</para>
            <para id="para-00068">Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00069">The correct answer is: The expression, which is a perfect square, is written as a squared expression.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_953b3ef1-2fe4-4336-945a-ca2aedee3adb" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00010">
            <para id="para-00070">What happened in Step 3?</para>
            <para id="para-00071">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00072">The quadratic term is written as a fraction so that it has a common denominator, which makes it easier to subtract.</para>
            <para id="para-00073">A random term was added to complete the square.</para>
            <para id="para-00074">The linear term is written as a fraction so that it has a common denominator, which makes it easier to subtract.</para>
            <para id="para-00075">The constant term is written as a fraction so that it has a common denominator, which makes it easier to subtract.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00010">
            <para id="para-00076">Correct! The constant term is written as a fraction so that it has a common denominator, which makes it easier to subtract.</para>
            <para id="para-00077">Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00078">The correct answer is: The constant term is written as a fraction so that it has a common denominator, which makes it easier to subtract.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="a043e713-3976-41a1-85a5-ba0bbb4f8b11" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00011">
            <para id="para-00079">What does the last expression tell us about the vertex of the graph of a function defined by this expression?</para>
            <para id="para-00080">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00081">The vertex of the graph is at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00082">The vertex of the graph is at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00083">The vertex of the graph is at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00084">The vertex of the graph is at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00011">
            <para id="para-00085">Correct! The vertex of the graph is at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00086">Try again. Revisit activities 9.10.3 and 9.10.6.</para>
            <para id="para-00087">The correct answer is: The vertex of the graph is at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_9c95eec7-1f50-47b2-b4a7-9799d8a2f05e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00012">
            <para><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00089">Enter the missing number, including the sign, for the expression when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>36</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> is written in vertex form.</para>
            <para id="para-00090">Enter the missing number, including the sign.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00012">
            <para id="para-00091">Correct! +6</para>
            <para id="para-00092">Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00093">The correct answer is +6.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_1a5fdedf-1462-4fae-bd8b-d5949c15dbcc" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00013">
            <para id="para-00094">Enter the missing number, including the sign.</para>
            <para id="para-00095">Enter the missing numbers, including the signs, for the expression when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>21</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> is written in vertex form. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:munder><m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi mathvariant="bold">a</m:mi><m:mo mathvariant="bold">.</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/></m:mrow><m:mo accent="true">―</m:mo></m:munder><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:munder><m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi mathvariant="bold">b</m:mi><m:mo mathvariant="bold">.</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/></m:mrow><m:mo accent="true">―</m:mo></m:munder></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00096">What is the value of the missing number, including the sign, in the place of the letter a?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00013">
            <para id="para-00097">Correct! +5</para>
            <para id="para-00098">Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00099">The correct answer is +5.</para>
